  "notes": "Cause code TBD in FORM-366 fields; block_13 empty in source, so no manufacturer/component reportable rows to model. 121 MDCLP auto start functioned as designed per Cooling Water system design (80 psig low header pressure setpoint) and is the reported consequence, not a failure. The root failure is the human-performance switching error on the 2RSY/2RSX disconnect switches, unrelated to the CL system itself, which only responded to the resulting bus loss. Previous similar event referenced only by an internal report identifier (L-PI-21-044); no formal LER number given, so used as literal key per instructions since no '#-YYYY-NNN' format was stated."
